§ `SCA-RTS Chapter I — General provisions`

-- ===========================================================================
-- Commission Delegated Regulation (EU) 2018/389, Chapter I, Articles 1 to 3.
-- OJ L 69, 13.3.2018, p. 23.
--
-- Article 1 states the subject matter and creates no testable rule; it is
-- quoted in NOTES.md rather than encoded. Articles 2 and 3 do bind, and the
-- Article 2 monitoring condition is the one every exemption in Chapter III
-- that is expressed "subject to compliance with the requirements laid down
-- in Article 2" depends on.
--
-- Source text: registers/source-bundle/reg-del-2018-389.txt
-- ===========================================================================

§§ `Article 2 — General authentication requirements`

-- Art 2(2): the five risk-based factors the monitoring mechanisms must take
-- into account "at a minimum". Encoded as a checklist because the exemptions
-- in Arts 10, 11, 12 and 15 are each conditioned on Article 2 compliance.
@ref "Regulation (EU) 2018/389, Art 2(2)"
GIVEN `lists of compromised or stolen authentication elements are used` IS A BOOLEAN
    , `the amount of each payment transaction is taken into account`    IS A BOOLEAN
    , `known fraud scenarios are taken into account`                    IS A BOOLEAN
    , `signs of malware infection in authentication sessions are taken into account` IS A BOOLEAN
    , `a log of provider-supplied access device or software use is kept` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the article 2(2) monitoring factors are all taken into account` IF
        `lists of compromised or stolen authentication elements are used`
    AND `the amount of each payment transaction is taken into account`
    AND `known fraud scenarios are taken into account`
    AND `signs of malware infection in authentication sessions are taken into account`
    AND `a log of provider-supplied access device or software use is kept`


§§ `Article 3 — Review of the security measures`

-- Art 3(2) second subparagraph: providers using the Article 18 exemption face
-- a yearly audit of the methodology, the model and the reported fraud rates.
@ref "Regulation (EU) 2018/389, Art 3(2)"
`minimum audit frequency in years for article 18 users` MEANS 1

-- Art 3(2): external independent auditor in the first year of use and at
-- least every 3 years thereafter.
@ref "Regulation (EU) 2018/389, Art 3(2)"
`maximum years between external audits for article 18 users` MEANS 3

@ref "Regulation (EU) 2018/389, Art 3(2)"
GIVEN `years since the external audit` IS A NUMBER
    , `first year of using the article 18 exemption` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an external independent audit is due` IF
        `first year of using the article 18 exemption`
    OR  `years since the external audit`
            AT LEAST `maximum years between external audits for article 18 users`



